1	# Gemini CLI MCP Server
2	
3	[![CI](https://github.com/DiversioTeam/gemini-cli-mcp/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/DiversioTeam/gemini-cli-mcp/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
4	[![codecov](https://codecov.io/gh/DiversioTeam/gemini-cli-mcp/branch/main/graph/badge.svg)](https://codecov.io/gh/DiversioTeam/gemini-cli-mcp)
5	[![Python 3.10-3.13](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10--3.13-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
6	[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
7	[![Ruff](https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/ruff/main/assets/badge/v2.json)](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff)
8	
9	A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that wraps the Gemini CLI, allowing AI assistants like Claude to use Gemini for research and analysis tasks.
10	
11	> **Disclaimer**: This is an unofficial, community-developed tool that wraps the Google Gemini CLI. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Google. All Google and Gemini trademarks, service marks, and logos are the property of Google LLC. This project is licensed under the MIT License.
12	
13	> **Important**: This tool requires that you have the Gemini CLI installed and authenticated on your system. See the [Prerequisites](#prerequisites) section for details.
14	
15	## Features
16	
17	- **gemini_prompt**: Send prompts to Gemini and get responses
18	- **gemini_research**: Research topics with optional file context
19	- **gemini_analyze_code**: Analyze code files for reviews, explanations, optimizations, security, or testing
20	- **gemini_summarize**: Summarize content from text or files
21	
22	## Installation
23	
24	### Quick Start (Recommended)
25	
26	```bash
27	# Install from GitHub (latest)
28	uvx --from git+https://github.com/DiversioTeam/gemini-cli-mcp gemini-mcp
29	
30	# Or from PyPI (when published)
31	uvx gemini-mcp
32	```
33	
34	### Development Installation
35	
36	```bash
37	git clone https://github.com/DiversioTeam/gemini-cli-mcp
38	cd gemini-cli-mcp
39	uv sync
40	uv run gemini-mcp
41	```
42	
43	## Prerequisites
44	
45	### 1. Python 3.10-3.13
46	Ensure you have Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12, or 3.13 installed. The project is tested on all these versions.
47	
48	### 2. Gemini CLI Installation and Authentication
49	
50	This MCP server requires the Gemini CLI to be installed and authenticated:
51	
52	1. **Install Gemini CLI**: Follow the official installation instructions for your platform
53	2. **Authenticate**: Run `gemini auth login` and follow the prompts
54	3. **Verify**: Test that it works by running `gemini -p "Hello, world!"`
55	
56	If you see an authentication error, make sure you've completed the login process.
57	
58	### 3. MCP-compatible Client
59	You'll need an MCP-compatible client such as:
60	- Claude Desktop
61	- Other MCP-compatible AI assistants
62	
63	## Usage
64	
65	### First Time Setup
66	
67	Before running the server, verify your setup:
68	
69	```bash
70	# Check if everything is configured correctly
71	gemini-mcp setup
72	```
73	
74	This will check:
75	- Gemini CLI installation
76	- Authentication status
77	- Environment configuration
78	
79	If you see authentication errors, run:
80	```bash
81	gemini auth login
82	```
83	
84	### Running the Server
85	
86	```bash
87	# Method 1: Run from current directory (for development)
88	uv run gemini-mcp
89	
90	# Method 2: Run using uvx from GitHub
91	uvx --from git+https://github.com/DiversioTeam/gemini-cli-mcp gemini-mcp
92	
93	# Method 3: Run if installed globally
94	gemini-mcp
95	
96	# With debug logging
97	LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG gemini-mcp
98	```
99	
100	### Configuring with Claude Code (CLI)
101	
102	#### Method 1: Using the CLI (Recommended)
103	
