148	
149	## Available Tools
150	
151	### gemini_prompt
152	Send a simple prompt to Gemini.
153	
154	**Parameters:**
155	- `prompt` (required): The prompt to send
156	- `model` (optional): The Gemini model to use (default: gemini-2.5-pro)
157	- `context` (optional): Additional context to prepend to the prompt
158	
159	### gemini_research
160	Research a topic with optional file context.
161	
162	**Parameters:**
163	- `topic` (required): The research topic or question
164	- `files` (optional): List of file paths to include as context
165	- `model` (optional): The Gemini model to use
166	
167	### gemini_analyze_code
168	Analyze code files for various purposes.
169	
170	**Parameters:**
171	- `files` (required): List of code files to analyze
172	- `analysis_type` (required): Type of analysis - one of:
173	  - `review`: Code review for issues and improvements
174	  - `explain`: Detailed explanation of the code
175	  - `optimize`: Performance and maintainability suggestions
176	  - `security`: Security vulnerability analysis
177	  - `test`: Test case suggestions
178	- `specific_question` (optional): Additional specific question
179	- `model` (optional): The Gemini model to use
180	
181	### gemini_summarize
182	Summarize content from text or files.
183	
184	**Parameters:**
185	- `content` (optional): Text content to summarize
186	- `files` (optional): Files to summarize (alternative to content)
187	- `summary_type` (optional): Type of summary - one of:
188	  - `brief`: 2-3 sentence summary (default)
189	  - `detailed`: Comprehensive summary
190	  - `bullet_points`: Bullet point format
191	  - `executive`: Executive summary for decision makers
192	- `model` (optional): The Gemini model to use
193	
194	Note: Either `content` or `files` must be provided.
195	
196	## Security
197	
198	This MCP server implements several security measures:
199	
200	### File Access Control
201	- **Sandboxed file access**: By default, file access is restricted to the current working directory
202	- **Path validation**: All file paths are validated to prevent directory traversal attacks
203	- **Configurable allowed directories**: You can specify allowed directories via:
204	  - Constructor parameter: `GeminiMCPServer(allowed_directories=["/path/to/safe/dir"])`
205	  - Environment variable: `GEMINI_MCP_ALLOWED_DIRS=/path1:/path2:/path3`
206	
207	### Input Sanitization
208	- All user inputs are properly sanitized before being passed to the CLI
209	- Command injection is prevented by using subprocess with argument lists (never shell=True)
210	- File paths are resolved and validated before use
211	
212	### Best Practices
213	- Always run the server with minimal required permissions
214	- Regularly update both the MCP server and Gemini CLI
215	- Monitor logs for any suspicious activity
216	
217	## Development
218	
