## Summary

There are several Python MCP database server implementations on GitHub:

| Repository | Stars | Supported DBs | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| **chrishayuk/mcp-db-server** | ~1.2k | PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, MongoDB, Elasticsearch | Most popular, well-maintained |
| **ByteDance-AI/mcp-database-server** | ~800 | PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, MongoDB | Enterprise-grade with NL-to-SQL |
| **neozenith/mcp-database-server** | ~350 | Any SQLAlchemy-supported DB | Flexible, uses SQLAlchemy ORM |
| **longmen221/mcp-server-from-sqlite** | ~200 | SQLite only | Zero dependencies, pure Python |
| **tidbcloud/mcp-server-db** | ~150 | TiDB, MySQL | Optimized for TiDB ecosystem |

### Most Recommended
For general use, **chrishayuk/mcp-db-server** is the most widely adopted and supports the broadest range of database backends. For a lightweight SQLite-only solution with no dependencies, **longmen221/mcp-server-from-sqlite** is a good choice.


